            "<strong>Decompress and protect:</strong> nasogastric tube on free drainage for vomiting, distension or obstruction; position of comfort (knees flexed); nothing on the abdomen — <strong>no heat</strong> (ruptures an inflamed appendix), <strong>no enema, no purgative, no 'abdominal massage'</strong>.",
